  m_text: "<u>Across: </u>\n1. A software update that fixes security flaws. \n6.
    Fake warnings designed to scare users into installing malware or paying money.
    \n8. A malicious software which encrypts victim's\u202Fdata and\u202Fdemands
    for Money. \n12. A cyber-attack that tricks users into downloading malware by
    offering something tempting or attractive.\n \n<u>Down: </u>\n2. Unwanted software
    that shows excessive ads. \n3. Type of phishing mails targeting specific individuals
    or enterprises.\u202F\n4. Getting into a restricted area by following someone
    without permission. \n5. AI-generated videos/audio used to impersonate someone.\u202F.
    \n7. A group of infected computers controlled by a hacker remotely.\n9. Faking
    a caller ID, or website to mislead victims. \n10. An abbreviated term for a secure
    Multiple Factor authentication. \n11. A computer virus named after a famous historical
    attack."
