  m_text: "<u>Across: </u>\n2. A secure Environment used to safely test suspicious
    files. \n7. A hidden part of the internet not shown on search engines. \n10.
    An attack where hackers inject malicious code into a legitimate web page that
    is frequented by their targets. \n11. An Abbreviation where cybercriminals impersonate
    business executives via email. \n14. An attack that overwhelms a system with
    traffic. \n16. A scam where attackers create a false story or identity to trick
    people into sharing information. \n17. A cyber-attack where someone secretly
    intercepts communication between two parties.\n18. A cyber-attack where an attacker
    sits between a user and a service to intercept and manipulate communication,
    often during login.\n \n<u>Down: </u>\n1. Malicious or uncontrolled AI systems
    that behave in harmful ways against their creators, users, or society.\n3. A
    scam where attackers offer a service or benefit in exchange for sensitive information..
    \n4. An act of secretly monitoring an organization to gather sensitive information.
    . \n5. A program that secretly records what you type.\n6. An attack that guesses
    passwords repeatedly. \n8. A scam where attackers use fake relationships or attraction
    to gain trust and extract information.  \n9. A software vulnerability unknown
    to its owners, developers or anyone capable of mitigating it. \n12. Malware that
    hides itself to avoid detection.\u202F\n13. Professionals who simulate real-world
    attacks to test an organization\u2019s security defences\n15. A cyber-attack
    where a fake login or browser window appears inside a real website to trick users. "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c946a736e068bed47ad4ce7c5353cfac, type: 2}
